## This is a Powang example file
## Arithmetics

## Operators
## + -> Sum       | also array concatenation and logical or for booleans.
## - -> Difference | also removes items from arrays and logical nand for booleans.
## * -> Product   | also repeats strings and arrays, counts ocurrences on strings.
## / -> Division  | floor division between integers, chunks strings and arrays,
##                | splits strings and logical nand for booleans.

## Integer arithmetic
## The four basic operations between integers always return an integer.
## Dividing by zero yields nova instead of throwing an error.
output(7 + 3); ## 10
output("\n");
output(7 - 3); ## 4
output("\n");
output(7 * 3); ## 21
output("\n");
output(7 / 3); ## 2 (floor division)
output("\n");
output(7 / 0); ## nova
output("\n");

## Number arithmetic
## Numbers are floating point values, division keeps the decimal part.
output(1.5 + 1); ## 2.5
output("\n");
output(7.0 / 2.0); ## 3.5
output("\n");

## Implicit casts on arithmetic
## An integer operand gets implicitly casted when the other side is a number.
printf("{0}\n", 2 + 0.5); ## 2 (untyped + casts the right operand to the left operand's type; use +: for typed addition)

## Boolean arithmetic
## true behaves like 1 and false like 0.
output(true + true); ## true
output("\n");
output(true - false); ## true
output("\n");
output(true * false); ## false
output("\n");

## String repetition and chunking
## Multiplying a string by an integer repeats it.
## Dividing a string by an integer chunks it into an array of that size.
## Dividing a string by a string splits it by the separator.
printf("{0}\n", "ab" * 3); ## ababab
output("abcd" / 2); ## [ab, cd]
output("\n");
output("a,b,c" / ","); ## [a, b, c]
output("\n");

## Array arithmetic
## Adding arrays concatenates them, subtracting an integer trims its tail
## and dividing by chunking takes an integer on the left side.
output([1 2] + [3 4]); ## 1, 2, 3, 4
output("\n");
output([1 2 3 4] - 2); ## 1, 2
output("\n");
output(2 / [1 2 3 4]); ## [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
output("\n");